IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `ei3-part3-premiums`

-- Tests of ei3-part3-premiums.l4 (Act ss 67 to 70).
-- Expected values are hand-worked from the text. The rate 1.63% (0.0163) and every other figure is invented for the test.

§ `s 67 the employee's premium`

#ASSERT `s 67 a person must pay the employee's premium` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 67 a person must pay the employee's premium` FALSE)
-- 40,000 of insurable earnings at 1.63% is 652 (40,000 x 0.0163).
#ASSERT `s 67 the employee's premium` 40_000 0.0163 EQUALS 652
-- 1,000 at 1.63% is 16.30; no earnings, no premium.
#ASSERT `s 67 the employee's premium` 1_000 0.0163 EQUALS 16.3
#ASSERT `s 67 the employee's premium` 0 0.0163 EQUALS 0
-- Section 67 states no cap: 100,000 of insurable earnings at 1.63% is 1,630, not the premium on the maximum yearly insurable earnings.
-- The maximum bites through s 82(2) (the employer stops deducting) and s 95 (the excess is an overpayment), not here.
#ASSERT `s 67 the employee's premium` 100_000 0.0163 EQUALS 1_630

§ `s 68 the employer's premium`

#ASSERT `s 68 the multiple of the employees' premiums that makes the employer's premium` EQUALS 1.4
-- 1.4 times 652 is 912.80.
#ASSERT `s 68 the employer's premium` 652 EQUALS 912.8
#ASSERT `s 68 the employer's premium` 0 EQUALS 0
-- Subject to s 69: a reduction of 100 under the regulations leaves 812.80; no reduction leaves 912.80.
#ASSERT `s 69 the employer's premium after the reduction` 652 100 EQUALS 812.8
#ASSERT `s 69 the employer's premium after the reduction` 652 0 EQUALS 912.8

§ `s 69(6) to (8) the reading rules, and the listed reasons`

#ASSERT `s 69(6) the payment is because of compassionate care` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 69(6) the payment is because of compassionate care` FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 69(7) the payment is because of a child's critical illness` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 69(7) the payment is because of a child's critical illness` FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 69(8) the payment is because of an adult's critical illness` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 69(8) the payment is because of an adult's critical illness` FALSE)
-- The first five reasons stand on their own words (the three section 23 flags are then irrelevant).
#ASSERT `s 69(1)(a) and (2) the payment is because of a listed reason` `ei3 illness` FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 69(1)(a) and (2) the payment is because of a listed reason` `ei3 injury` FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 69(1)(a) and (2) the payment is because of a listed reason` `ei3 quarantine` FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 69(1)(a) and (2) the payment is because of a listed reason` `ei3 pregnancy` FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 69(1)(a) and (2) the payment is because of a listed reason` `ei3 child care` FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Compassionate care, a child's and an adult's critical illness are read through their own section 23 flag only.
#ASSERT `s 69(1)(a) and (2) the payment is because of a listed reason` `ei3 compassionate care` TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 69(1)(a) and (2) the payment is because of a listed reason` `ei3 compassionate care` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 69(1)(a) and (2) the payment is because of a listed reason` `ei3 a child's critical illness` FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 69(1)(a) and (2) the payment is because of a listed reason` `ei3 a child's critical illness` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 69(1)(a) and (2) the payment is because of a listed reason` `ei3 an adult's critical illness` FALSE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 69(1)(a) and (2) the payment is because of a listed reason` `ei3 an adult's critical illness` TRUE TRUE FALSE)

§ `s 69(1) a system for reducing the employer's premium`

-- (b): 5/12 of a reduction of 1,200 is 500. Exactly 500 is "at least equal"; one cent under is not.
#ASSERT `s 69(1)(b) the insured persons will benefit by at least 5/12 of the reduction` 500 1_200
#ASSERT NOT (`s 69(1)(b) the insured persons will benefit by at least 5/12 of the reduction` 499.99 1_200)
#ASSERT `s 69(1)(b) the insured persons will benefit by at least 5/12 of the reduction` 600 1_200
#ASSERT `s 69(1)(b) the insured persons will benefit by at least 5/12 of the reduction` 0 0
-- Arguments: listed reason; plan covers insured persons of the employer; plan under a provincial law; effect of reducing the
-- special benefits; the insured persons' benefit; the reduction.
#ASSERT `s 69(1) a system for reducing the employer's premium is to be provided` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE 500 1_200
-- A plan established under a provincial law falls under subsection (2) instead.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 69(1) a system for reducing the employer's premium is to be provided` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 500 1_200)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 69(1) a system for reducing the employer's premium is to be provided` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE 500 1_200)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 69(1) a system for reducing the employer's premium is to be provided` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE 500 1_200)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 69(1) a system for reducing the employer's premium is to be provided` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 500 1_200)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 69(1) a system for reducing the employer's premium is to be provided` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE 499 1_200)

§ `s 69(2) provincial plans`

-- Arguments: under a provincial law for a listed reason; paid to insured persons and reduces/eliminates their special benefits;
-- paid to self-employed persons and reduces/eliminates their benefits.
#ASSERT `s 69(2) the premiums a system must reduce` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST `ei3 the employer's and the employee's premiums`
#ASSERT `s 69(2) the premiums a system must reduce` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST `ei3 the premiums under Part VII.1`
#ASSERT `s 69(2) the premiums a system must reduce` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST `ei3 all those premiums`
-- Nobody's benefits reduced, or not a provincial law: the subsection calls for no reduction (not covered).
#ASSERT `s 69(2) the premiums a system must reduce` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 69(2) the premiums a system must reduce` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 69(4) and (5) late applications and reconsideration`

-- Prescribed time 31 March 2025. A late application within 36 months (to 31 March 2028) with good cause and the prescribed conditions.
#ASSERT `s 69(4) the Commission may regard the application as made at the prescribed time` (YearMonthDay 2025 3 31) (YearMonthDay 2025 4 1) TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `s 69(4) the Commission may regard the application as made at the prescribed time` (YearMonthDay 2025 3 31) (YearMonthDay 2028 3 31) TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 69(4) the Commission may regard the application as made at the prescribed time` (YearMonthDay 2025 3 31) (YearMonthDay 2028 4 1) TRUE TRUE)
-- Made on the prescribed day itself, it is not late: this rule is about late applications.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 69(4) the Commission may regard the application as made at the prescribed time` (YearMonthDay 2025 3 31) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 31) TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 69(4) the Commission may regard the application as made at the prescribed time` (YearMonthDay 2025 3 31) (YearMonthDay 2025 6 1) FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 69(4) the Commission may regard the application as made at the prescribed time` (YearMonthDay 2025 3 31) (YearMonthDay 2025 6 1) TRUE FALSE)
-- add months clamps: 36 months after 29 February 2024 is 28 February 2027.
#ASSERT `s 69(4) the Commission may regard the application as made at the prescribed time` (YearMonthDay 2024 2 29) (YearMonthDay 2027 2 28) TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 69(4) the Commission may regard the application as made at the prescribed time` (YearMonthDay 2024 2 29) (YearMonthDay 2027 3 1) TRUE TRUE)
-- Reconsideration within 36 months after the date of the decision (15 June 2025 to 15 June 2028).
#ASSERT `s 69(5) the Commission may reconsider the decision` (YearMonthDay 2025 6 15) (YearMonthDay 2028 6 15)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 69(5) the Commission may reconsider the decision` (YearMonthDay 2025 6 15) (YearMonthDay 2028 6 16))
#ASSERT `s 69(5) the new decision applies in place of the reconsidered decision` (YearMonthDay 2025 6 15) (YearMonthDay 2027 1 1)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 69(5) the new decision applies in place of the reconsidered decision` (YearMonthDay 2025 6 15) (YearMonthDay 2028 6 16))

§ `s 70 overlapping pay periods`

-- Earnings of 2025 employment paid on 5 January 2026 belong to 2026; paid on 31 December 2025 they stay in 2025.
#ASSERT `s 70 the year in which the insurable employment is deemed to have occurred` 2025 (YearMonthDay 2026 1 5) EQUALS JUST 2026
#ASSERT `s 70 the year in which the insurable employment is deemed to have occurred` 2025 (YearMonthDay 2025 12 31) EQUALS JUST 2025
-- Paid before the year of the employment: the section is silent (not covered).
#ASSERT `s 70 the year in which the insurable employment is deemed to have occurred` 2025 (YearMonthDay 2024 12 31) EQUALS NOTHING
